// Site configuration: executor/container setup only.
// Native Nextflow: -profile slurm,apptainer -c site.config
// Managed: --profile slurm,apptainer --site-config site.config
// Put task requests and queue mappings in --resource-config resources.json.
// The generic resource example leaves queue/account unset; Dardel users can
// copy resources.dardel.json (shared allocation) and supply their own account.
// Do not assign a whole-node partition globally to serial QC tasks.
//
// Native Nextflow users may set site options here, for example:
// params.slurm_account = 'YOUR_ACCOUNT'
// params.slurm_partition = 'YOUR_SHARED_PARTITION'
// process { withName: '(^|.*:)NETWORK_FIT' { memory = '96 GB' } }
//
// Other schedulers: configure process.executor and their native account options.
// No automatic queue switch, exclusive-node flag or concurrency cap is imposed.
